Overlay patch 0065 (D-084): REAL-TIME TICK CATCH-UP + the pace probe.

THE SYMPTOM (the user, 2026-10-08, iPhone Air, 120 Hz): frame rate dips into
the 90s and THE MUSIC SLOWS DOWN.

THE MECHANISM. Graph_ProcessGfxCommands runs ONE game tick and then renders
`count` interpolated frames for it, count = interpolation fps / tick rate
(120 / 20 = 6). Every one of those frames blocks on the display. Nothing in
the loop looks at the wall clock, so a frame that misses its vsync does not
drop a frame -- it stretches the TICK. Audio is lock-step with the tick
(Graph_ProcessGfxCommands hands the audio thread one tick's worth of synthesis
and waits for it), so the sequencer's tempo IS the tick rate: six frames at
120 Hz = 50 ms = 20 Hz; one 16.7 ms frame among them makes it 58 ms = 17 Hz =
the music 14 % slow. The device log shows it in every bad window: sim_tps
tracks fps / 6 exactly (fps 105 -> sim_tps 17.5; fps 67 -> 11.2).

THE FIX. Keep a debt: real time elapsed minus ticks x tick period (clamped to
[0, one tick]; a stall over 250 ms -- a load, a background, a menu hitch --
resets it, so the game never fast-forwards through a pause). While the debt
is at least one frame period, drop that many of THIS tick's EARLIEST
interpolated frames (never the last one, which is the tick's real state).
Skipping frames shortens the tick, which pays the debt back on the next
measurement, so nothing double-counts. Game time and audio stay at 20 Hz;
only the frame count falls, which is what a missed frame should cost.
gSohIos.TickCatchup (default 1) is the A/B switch. VR / 3D are left alone
(the compositor paces those). The gfx debugger path still overrides count.

THE PROBE (no behaviour change): one `SOH_PACE` line per 10 s, beside
SOH_PERF, splitting each 2D frame into
  wait  -- time inside SetupScreenFramebuffer (nextDrawable / background park)
  busy  -- drawable acquired -> SwapBuffersBegin (ImGui, Fast3D interpret,
           texture loads, commit): the game thread's own CPU work
  sleep -- LUS's SyncFramerateWithTime nanosleep pacer
plus tick wall p50/p95/max, frames skipped, ticks that skipped, debt, and
thermal + power state (Low Power Mode caps the panel at 60 Hz -- with 6
frames per tick that alone would halve the game's speed -- and charging heats
the phone before thermalState moves).
SOH_PERF's eng_ms is wait+busy+sleep and cannot say which; this can.
gSohIos.PaceStressMs (default 0, test instrument only) busy-waits that many
ms inside each frame, so the catch-up can be proven on a simulator.

Generate against a vendor tree with 0001..0064 applied and 0065 not applied.
Every hunk sits outside the hunks (and 3-line contexts) of 0008/0045/0016 so
the whole series stays reversible.


